meta {
  name: Configure the events template
  type: http
  seq: 8
}

patch {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/templates/{{barcelonaComedyClubEventsTemplateId}}
  body: json
  auth: inherit
}

body:json {
  {
    "action": "POST",
    "url": "https://barcelonacomedyclub.com/wp-json/eventon/v1/data?action=init",
    "body": "action=eventon_init_load&cals[c1][sc][calendar_type]=default&cals[c1][sc][number_of_months]=6&cals[c1][sc][event_past_future]=future&cals[c1][sc][lang]=L1",
    "headers": {
      "Content-Type": "application/x-www-form-urlencoded; charset=UTF-8",
      "Accept": "application/json"
    }
  }
}

tests {
  test("returns 200", function () {
    expect(res.status).to.equal(200);
  });
}

docs {
  The homepage's "#entradas" section is an EventON weekly calendar that
  loads its events after the page, so the HTML has none. This template
  asks EventON for them directly, the way the calendar's own script does
  (`init_load_cal_data`), through its REST route: a form POST, no login
  and no nonce, answered as `application/json` (the `admin-ajax.php`
  alternative answers JSON labelled `text/html`, which the engine would
  parse as a page).

  The form asks for a list calendar instead of the site's weekly one:
  `calendar_type=default`, `number_of_months=6` from the current month,
  `event_past_future=future`. That is every upcoming date over six months
  (82 today, 7 shows), with no month or year fixed, so scheduled runs
  always start at the current month.
}
